Subject: [PATCH] Fix build-breaking extra closing div in leak-map-schedule.tsx
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The master-detail rewrite left one stray extra </div> right after the
timeline list, closing the grid wrapper a level early instead of just
the left column — the right column then ended up outside the grid, and
the file ran one </div> short at the end. Turbopack reported this as
"Unterminated regexp literal" (the desynced tag matching eventually
misreads a later "/" as regex), not as the real mismatched-tag error.

My earlier "balance check" only counted {} and () — it never actually
validated JSX tag matching, which is exactly the class of bug this was.
Verified this fix with a real open/close tag count instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
---
 src/app/dashboard/engagements/[id]/leak-map-schedule.tsx | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/app/dashboard/engagements/[id]/leak-map-schedule.tsx b/src/app/dashboard/engagements/[id]/leak-map-schedule.tsx
index fa1f9f0..a584cff 100644
--- a/src/app/dashboard/engagements/[id]/leak-map-schedule.tsx
+++ b/src/app/dashboard/engagements/[id]/leak-map-schedule.tsx
@@ -412,7 +412,6 @@ export function LeakMapSchedule({ engagementId }: { engagementId: string }) {
                 ))}
               </div>
             )}
-          </div>
         </div>
 
